{"title":"Career Roadmap · Government Architect","role":"Government Architect","summary":"A Government Architect works on the planning, design, documentation, execution, conservation, and management of public buildings and government infrastructure.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Arch (Bachelor of Architecture)","Course":"Architecture"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Government Architect works on the planning, design, documentation, execution, conservation, and management of public buildings and government infrastructure."},{"type":"p","text":"Typical projects may include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Government offices and administrative complexes"},{"text":"Schools, colleges, hospitals, and healthcare facilities"},{"text":"Courts and institutional buildings"},{"text":"Police and emergency-service facilities"},{"text":"Housing and public residential projects"},{"text":"Transport terminals and public amenities"},{"text":"Cultural and heritage buildings"},{"text":"Government campuses"},{"text":"Urban-development projects"},{"text":"Public spaces and community infrastructure"},{"text":"Renovation, retrofitting, and adaptive reuse"}]},{"type":"flow","items":["The role combines architecture","public-sector regulations","building codes","project management","procurement","construction administration","urban planning","sustainability."],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"A Government Architect may work through government architecture departments, public works organizations, urban-development authorities, municipal bodies, housing boards, infrastructure agencies, public-sector organizations, or other government institutions."},{"type":"note","label":"Important","text":"Exact government post names, recruitment routes, eligibility, registration requirements, examinations, and age criteria vary by organization and can change. Always verify the current official recruitment notification and applicable architectural-registration rules."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Stage","Primary Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"B.Arch + Foundation"},{"text":"Architecture, building technology, codes, BIM, documentation"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Entry Government Architect / Architectural Professional"},{"text":"Public projects, documentation, site supervision, approvals"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Senior Architect / Project Lead"},{"text":"Large public projects, project management, planning"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Senior Government Architecture Leadership"},{"text":"Policy, major infrastructure, institutional planning, design governance"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to Build During B.Arch","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Architectural Foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Build strong fundamentals rather than focusing only on software."},{"type":"h","text":"Core subjects"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Architectural design"},{"text":"Design principles"},{"text":"Architectural graphics"},{"text":"History of architecture"},{"text":"Building materials"},{"text":"Basic structures"},{"text":"Environmental studies"},{"text":"Site planning"},{"text":"Human dimensions"},{"text":"Spatial planning"},{"text":"Architectural representation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Technical skills"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AutoCAD"},{"text":"SketchUp"},{"text":"Photoshop"},{"text":"Illustrator/InDesign"},{"text":"Basic rendering"},{"text":"Hand drafting"},{"text":"Architectural model making"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Government relevance"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop the ability to understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Site constraints"},{"text":"Building functions"},{"text":"Public circulation"},{"text":"Accessibility"},{"text":"Fire safety"},{"text":"Basic building regulations"},{"text":"Climate-responsive design"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Building Technology + Documentation"},{"type":"p","text":"Government architecture involves significantly more documentation and compliance than studio design alone."},{"type":"h","text":"Focus areas"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Building construction"},{"text":"Structural systems"},{"text":"RCC construction"},{"text":"Steel construction"},{"text":"Masonry"},{"text":"Waterproofing"},{"text":"Doors/windows"},{"text":"Building services"},{"text":"Plumbing"},{"text":"Electrical systems"},{"text":"HVAC"},{"text":"Fire safety"},{"text":"Accessibility"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Documentation"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to produce:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Plans"},{"text":"Sections"},{"text":"Elevations"},{"text":"Working drawings"},{"text":"Construction details"},{"text":"Door/window schedules"},{"text":"Material schedules"},{"text":"Area statements"},{"text":"Specifications"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Software"},{"type":"p","text":"Target:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AutoCAD — Advanced"},{"text":"Revit — Intermediate"},{"text":"SketchUp — Advanced"},{"text":"Photoshop — Intermediate"},{"text":"InDesign — Intermediate"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Public Architecture + Regulations"},{"type":"p","text":"This is where the Government Architect profile should become more specialized."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Building bye-laws"},{"text":"Development regulations"},{"text":"Zoning"},{"text":"FAR/FSI"},{"text":"Setbacks"},{"text":"Ground coverage"},{"text":"Parking requirements"},{"text":"Accessibility standards"},{"text":"Fire-safety requirements"},{"text":"Environmental requirements"},{"text":"Universal design"},{"text":"Public-building planning"},{"text":"Institutional architecture"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Public-sector project types"},{"type":"p","text":"Study the design requirements of:"},{"type":"h","text":"Education"},{"type":"flow","items":["Schools","Colleges","Unive